    <string name="source_verification_title">Source verification · %1$s</string>
    <string name="source_verification_verified_body">%1$s has a locally pinned publisher key, and the recorded signer matches that pin. This verifies publisher continuity for this device; it does not certify the source or prove Google\'s developer-registration status.</string>
    <string name="source_verification_unverified_body">%1$s does not have a locally pinned publisher key for this package yet, or its observed signer differs from the pin. Review the APK evidence before trusting it. The normal Android install confirmation still controls whether installation proceeds.</string>
    <string name="source_verification_unknown_body">LocalAndroidStore does not yet have enough package or signer evidence for %1$s to classify this source. Inspecting the APK supplies the missing local evidence.</string>
    <string name="source_verification_google_unknown">Google developer registration is a separate system decision. Android exposes that result to the system installer, not to LocalAndroidStore. If Android requires the advanced sideloading flow, it includes its own safeguards and may impose a one-day waiting period.</string>
